    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0961" n="865" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg865"/>

                <head>No. 386.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gibbs to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-04-01"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 1, 1879</date>.
                        (Received May 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 328.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 5th instant I received a circular
                    note from the Peruvian Government, of which I inclose a copy and translation, in
                    reference to <pb facs="0962" n="866" xml:id="pg866"/> the status of American
                    vessels, what constitutes nationality, and if foreign vessels have the right to
                    carry the American flag.</p>
                <p>I have answered this day as per copy annexed.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RICHARD GIBBS.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d415-a1.xml" xpointer="d415-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d415-a2.xml" xpointer="d415-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
